(O111 - Calibrate Tool Setter Height)
(Step 1 of tool setter setup:)
(Uses a known reference (gauge block or bare spindle nose))
(to establish the tool setter surface Z position.)
(Writes result to [TOOL_SETTER]REF_Z via G10 L2)
(Call as: O111 call [reference_height])
(Example: O111 call [50.0] for a 50mm gauge block)

O111 sub

    #<ref_height> = #1
    #<setter_x> = #<_ini[TOOL_SETTER]X>
    #<setter_y> = #<_ini[TOOL_SETTER]Y>
    #<setter_vel> = #<_ini[TOOL_SETTER]VEL>
    #<max_depth> = #<_ini[TOOL_SETTER]MAX_PROBE_DEPTH>
    #<z_safe> = #<_ini[PROBE]Z_SAFE>

    M5
    M9
    G90
    G40
    G49

    (Move to tool setter)
    G53 G0 Z#<z_safe>
    G53 G0 X#<setter_x> Y#<setter_y>

    (Probe down to find setter surface)
    G91
    G38.2 Z[0 - #<max_depth>] F[#<setter_vel> * 4]
    G0 Z2.0
    G38.2 Z-4.0 F#<setter_vel>

    (The probed Z position is where the setter surface is)
    (relative to machine coordinates. We need to store)
    (this as the reference for future tool measurements.)
    #<setter_surface_z> = #5063

    (Store as reference: REF_Z = setter_surface_z - ref_height)
    (This way, when a tool probes the setter, the length)
    (is calculated as: probed_z - REF_Z = actual tool length)
    #<new_ref_z> = [#<setter_surface_z> - #<ref_height>]

    (Write to INI using G10 L2 - but G10 L2 sets work offsets,)
    (not INI values. We need to use a different approach.)
    (For now, just report the value so the operator can)
    (enter it in the Settings tab or INI file.)

    (MSG, ========================================)
    (MSG, Tool Setter Calibration Complete)
    (MSG, Setter surface probed at Z: #<setter_surface_z>)
    (MSG, Reference height used: #<ref_height>)
    (MSG, Calculated REF_Z: #<new_ref_z>)
    (MSG, )
    (MSG, Enter this value in Settings -> Probing ->)
    (MSG, Tool Setter Reference Z, or update the INI:)
    (MSG, [TOOL_SETTER] REF_Z = #<new_ref_z>)
    (MSG, ========================================)

    (Retract)
    G53 G0 Z#<z_safe>

O111 endsub
M2
